# Trivy ignore file for dev container images.
#
# Every entry here is a *fixed* CVE that the publish gate would otherwise block
# on but which is not exploitable in these images' actual usage. Entries are
# grouped by carrier; each group documents the carrier, why the vulnerable path
# is not exercised, and the condition under which the entry should be removed.
#
# NOT listed here, by design:
#   - linux-libc-dev (kernel-header) findings — dropped categorically by
#     .trivy/ignore-policy.rego (containers use the host kernel, not the baked-in
#     headers). Do NOT re-add kernel CVEs here; the rego covers them permanently.
#   - status=affected (no-fix) CVEs — ignore-unfixed (trivy.yaml) already keeps
#     them from gating. Only fixed findings belong in this file.
#
# Last audited: 2026-10-21 (issue #629). All 14 images in the current publish
# set were built locally from scratch (--no-cache) on arm64: the 13 entries of
# docker/versions/matrix.json plus dev-base. Each was scanned with Trivy 0.72.0
# (as in the CD arm64 step) without this file or the rego, keeping only
# ignore-unfixed and skip-files from trivy.yaml. Every entry below appeared in
# at least one of those scans, so none was removed. The audit corrected the
# carrier notes: gh (2.103.0, go1.27.3, x/net v0.60.0, x/mod v0.41.0) no longer
# carries any entry, the image's Go is 1.26.10, and golangci-lint no longer
# carries CVE-2026-56852. No carrier had a newer upstream release to bump to. With this file and the rego,
# all 14 images scan clean (0 HIGH/CRITICAL).
# Previous audits: 2026-10-16 (issue #605), which removed 25 stale entries, and
# 2026-08-15 (issue #561), which removed 137.
# When re-auditing, an entry is stale if it no longer appears in a fresh scan of
# the current images (see issue #561 for the method).
#
# go-licenses notes below refer to the binary that `go install
# github.com/google/go-licenses/v2@latest` (v2.0.1) produces with the image's
# go1.26.10. `go tool nm` on that binary (issue #629) shows that the only
# packages it links from its own module requirements are
# golang.org/x/net/context/ctxhttp, golang.org/x/mod/semver and
# golang.org/x/text/{cases,internal,language,transform,unicode/norm}. The
# x/net/http2/hpack, x/net/idna, x/net/dns/dnsmessage and x/net/http packages it
# also contains are the Go standard library's vendored copies
# (vendor/golang.org/x/net/...), which come from the patched go1.26.10.

# =============================================================================
# Go stdlib in actionlint 1.7.12 (all images). actionlint is the newest release
# (2026-03-30) and is built with go1.26.1. Trivy scores Go stdlib
# vulnerabilities by the toolchain version baked into each binary, with no
# import-reachability analysis, so every stdlib CVE fixed since go1.26.1 gates
# this binary until upstream re-releases it with a patched Go. actionlint is a
# static linter of local workflow files: it makes no network connections, and
# the affected stdlib paths (crypto/x509 hostname check, encoding/asn1,
# encoding/xml, net/url, net/http h2c, crypto/tls, html/template, os.Root, MIME
# header decode) are not exercised on untrusted input.
#
# As of the 2026-10-21 audit (issue #629), actionlint is the only stdlib carrier
# of every entry in this block. CVE-2026-33814 is also reported against
# go-licenses (go image) through golang.org/x/net v0.43.0 (fixed in 0.53.0).
# It is in the HTTP/2 transport, and go-licenses links no HTTP/2 code from its
# x/net module (see the go-licenses note in the header).
#
# Remove once an actionlint release is built with a Go that fixes them (and, for
# CVE-2026-33814, once go-licenses requires x/net >= 0.53.0). The daily
# upstream-refresh PR picks up a new actionlint.
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-27145
CVE-2026-32280
CVE-2026-32281
CVE-2026-32283
CVE-2026-33810
CVE-2026-33811
CVE-2026-33814
CVE-2026-33818
CVE-2026-39820
CVE-2026-39822
CVE-2026-39836
CVE-2026-42499
CVE-2026-42504
CVE-2026-56853
CVE-2026-56858
CVE-2026-56859
CVE-2026-56860
CVE-2026-56862

# Go 1.26.9 / 1.27.2 batch (issue #605). Fixed in Go 1.26.9 / 1.27.2, but the
# newest upstream release of each of these carriers is still built with an
# older Go (carriers as of the 2026-10-21 audit, issue #629):
#   - actionlint 1.7.12, go1.26.1 (all images)
#   - shfmt 3.14.1, go1.27.1 (all images)
#   - tofu 1.13.9 (dev-base): CVE-2026-78669 only, via golang.org/x/net
#     v0.57.0. tofu is built with go1.27.3, so its stdlib is fixed. (1.13.9,
#     bumped under issue #755, still requires x/net v0.57.0.)
#   - go-licenses v2.0.1 (dev-go): CVE-2026-78669 only, via golang.org/x/net
#     v0.43.0. It is built with the image's go1.26.10, so its stdlib is fixed.
# gh, nfpm and trivy carried them too. gh 2.103.0 is built with go1.27.3 and
# x/net v0.60.0, and the nfpm 2.48.0 and trivy 0.76.1 bumps fixed theirs, so
# those carriers are not ignored.
#
# CVE-2026-78667 — net/http: CPU exhaustion parsing Range headers in
#   FileServer / ServeContent / ServeFile. Server-side only. None of these
#   binaries serves files over HTTP.
# CVE-2026-97031 — crypto/tls: memory exhaustion from repeated ECH outer
#   extension references in a ClientHello. Server-side handshake only. None of
#   these binaries accepts TLS connections.
# CVE-2026-78669 — net/http HTTP/2: CPU exhaustion from repeated
#   SETTINGS_INITIAL_WINDOW_SIZE frames. Also carried as golang.org/x/net/http2
#   < 0.60.0 in tofu (v0.57.0) and go-licenses (v0.43.0). Unlike the two above,
#   this one affects HTTP/2 clients too, and tofu (provider and module
#   registries) is an HTTP/2 client. Triggering it requires the
#   TLS-authenticated server itself to be malicious, and the impact is CPU
#   exhaustion of a short-lived, user-invoked CLI process, with no
#   confidentiality or integrity impact. actionlint and shfmt make no network
#   connections. go-licenses links no x/net/http2 code
#   from its x/net module (see the go-licenses note in the header), so it
#   cannot run the vulnerable flow-control path.
#
# Remove each once actionlint and shfmt both ship
# builds with Go >= 1.26.9 / 1.27.2, and tofu and go-licenses require x/net
# >= 0.60.0. The daily upstream-refresh PR and the nightly rebuild pick these up.
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-78669
CVE-2026-97031

# Go 1.26.10 / 1.27.3 batch (issue #624). CVE-2026-111943 — crypto/x509:
# mitigation for a specific Certificate Authority. Go 1.26.10 / 1.27.3 (released
# 2026-10-20) add a denylist, so Certificate.Verify filters out any chain that
# contains one of a small set of intermediate certificates the Go team no longer
# trusts. Older binaries still accept a chain through those intermediates when
# the system trust store does.
#
# tofu and trivy carried it too. The tofu 1.13.2 and trivy 0.76.1 bumps fix
# them (both are built with go1.27.3), so those carriers are not ignored. The
# newest upstream release of each carrier below is still built with an older
# Go (`go version` on the downloaded release binaries, 2026-10-21; confirmed by
# the issue #629 scans):
#   - actionlint 1.7.12, go1.26.1 (all images). A static linter of local
#     workflow files. It makes no network connections and verifies no
#     certificates.
#   - shfmt 3.14.1, go1.27.1 (all images). A local shell formatter. It makes no
#     network connections.
#   - nfpm 2.48.0, go1.27.2 (all images). Assembles .deb/.rpm packages from
#     local files. It makes no TLS connections in this use.
#   - scorecard 5.6.0, go1.27.2 (dev-base). An HTTPS client of the GitHub API
#     only. Exploiting the missing denylist needs a man-in-the-middle holding a
#     certificate that chains through one of the distrusted intermediates. The
#     impact would be tampered scorecard output.
#
# Remove once actionlint, shfmt, nfpm and scorecard
# all ship builds with Go >= 1.26.10 / 1.27.3. The daily upstream-refresh PR and the
# nightly rebuild pick these up.
CVE-2026-111943

# =============================================================================
# Go's x/net idna and dnsmessage code. CVE-2026-39821 is in IDNA Punycode label
# handling (fixed in Go 1.26.6 and x/net 0.55.0). CVE-2026-46600 is a panic when
# parsing an invalid SVCB/HTTPS DNS record (fixed in Go 1.26.6 and x/net
# 0.56.0). Carriers as of the 2026-10-21 audit (issue #629):
#   - actionlint 1.7.12 (all images), as a stdlib finding: go1.26.1 predates
#     the fix in the standard library's vendored copy of x/net. actionlint
#     resolves no DNS names and normalizes no hostnames; it makes no network
#     connections.
#   - go-licenses v2.0.1 (dev-go), via golang.org/x/net v0.43.0. go-licenses
#     links neither x/net/idna nor x/net/dns/dnsmessage from that module; the
#     copies in the binary are the standard library's, from the patched
#     go1.26.10 (see the go-licenses note in the header).
# Remove once an actionlint release is built with Go >= 1.26.6 and go-licenses
# requires x/net >= 0.56.0.
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-46600

# golang.org/x/net/html (go image only). Both CVEs are in the HTML parser
# (DOCTYPE character references, duplicate attributes). The only carrier is
# go-licenses v2.0.1 (x/net v0.43.0, the newest release), confirmed by the
# 2026-10-21 audit (issue #629). x/net/html is not linked into that binary
# (`go tool nm` shows no x/net/html symbols), and go-licenses never parses HTML.
# Remove once go-licenses requires x/net >= 0.55.0.
CVE-2026-25681
CVE-2026-27136

# golang.org/x/net/html < 0.62.0 in prebuilt Go CLIs (all images), fixed in
# x/net 0.62.0 (released 2026-10-27). Issue #755; first gated the 2026-11-07
# CD run and nightly. CVE-2026-78661 (GO-2026-6860) — quadratic CPU and
# allocation in the HTML tree builder: when it coalesces adjacent text nodes
# (parser.addText, parser.fosterParent), it re-copies the accumulated string on
# every token, so input with many short text runs separated by ignored end
# tags costs O(n^2). The advisory's affected symbols are Parse, ParseFragment,
# ParseWithOptions, ParseFragmentWithOptions and the parser internals; the
# tokenizer is not affected.
# Carriers, each the newest upstream release (checked 2026-11-07). The x/net
# version is the build info in the binary; the linked x/net/html functions are
# the function names in the binary (both read with `strings` on the amd64
# release binary, and on the binaries in the published dev-go:1.27 image for
# gh and go-licenses):
#   - /usr/bin/gh 2.103.3 (all images), x/net v0.60.0. Links only the
#     tokenizer (NewTokenizer, Tokenizer methods, EscapeString, unescape).
#   - /usr/local/bin/nfpm 2.48.0 (all images), x/net v0.60.0. Links no
#     x/net/html code (only x/net/context, proxy and internal/socks).
#   - /usr/local/bin/scorecard 5.6.0 (base), x/net v0.60.0. Links only
#     x/net/html's package init and x/net/html/charset.
#   - /usr/local/bin/tofu 1.13.9 (base), x/net v0.57.0. Links no x/net/html
#     code.
#   - go-licenses v2.0.1 (go images), x/net v0.43.0. Links no x/net/html code
#     (see the go-licenses note in the header).
# None of these binaries contains Parse, ParseFragment, ParseWithOptions,
# ParseFragmentWithOptions or the parser's addText / fosterParent / parse, so
# the vulnerable tree builder cannot run. Trivy flags the module version only.
# trivy carried it too (0.76.1, x/net v0.60.0). The trivy 0.76.2 bump (issue
# #755) ships x/net v0.62.0, so that carrier is not ignored.
# Not fixable by bumping: no newer release of any carrier above exists, and
# each one's newest release still requires x/net < 0.62.0. Remove per carrier
# once a release requires x/net >= 0.62.0. The daily upstream-refresh PR picks
# up nfpm, scorecard and tofu; every image build installs the
# newest gh from the cli.github.com apt repository and runs `go install
# github.com/google/go-licenses/v2@latest`.
CVE-2026-78661

# golang.org/x/text v0.28.0 in go-licenses v2.0.1 (go image only), fixed in
# 0.39.0. As of the 2026-10-21 audit (issue #629) go-licenses is the only
# carrier; golangci-lint now requires x/text v0.41.0. CVE-2026-56852: a
# norm.Iter can loop forever on input that contains invalid UTF-8. Unlike the
# x/net packages above, x/text/unicode/norm from the module is linked into
# go-licenses (`go tool nm`). go-licenses runs on the developer's own module
# and its dependency tree, not on attacker-supplied text, and the impact is a
# hang of a short-lived, user-invoked CLI with no confidentiality or integrity
# impact. Not fixable by rebuilding: both the newest release (v2.0.1) and the
# master branch still require x/text v0.28.0. Remove once a go-licenses
# release requires x/text >= 0.39.0.
CVE-2026-56852

# golang.org/x/text v0.28.0 in go-licenses v2.0.1 (go image only), fixed in
# 0.41.0. Issue #624. CVE-2026-56851: the secure/precis Nickname profile can
# panic with an out-of-bounds slice error when it transforms crafted input into
# a short destination buffer. The vulnerable package is not in the binary:
# `go tool nm` on a fresh `go install github.com/google/go-licenses/v2@latest`
# shows no x/text/secure/precis symbols (re-checked in issue #629). Its x/text
# packages are listed in the go-licenses note in the header.
# Not fixable by rebuilding: `go install` builds with go-licenses' own go.mod,
# and both the newest release (v2.0.1) and the master branch still require
# x/text v0.28.0. Remove once a go-licenses release requires x/text >= 0.41.0.
CVE-2026-56851

# golang.org/x/image (go image only). The carrier is go-test-coverage v2.19.0,
# which pulls x/image v0.41.0 in through its coverage-badge renderer. Issue
# #606; re-checked in issue #629.
# CVE-2026-46602 — x/image/tiff decoder DoS (fixed in 0.43.0).
# CVE-2026-46603 — x/image/vp8l (WebP lossless) excessive allocation (fixed in
#   0.45.0).
# Neither vulnerable package is in the binary: the only x/image packages linked
# into go-test-coverage are x/image/font and x/image/math/fixed
# (`go tool nm` shows no x/image/tiff, vp8l or webp symbols), so the TIFF and
# VP8L decoders cannot run.
# Not fixable by bumping: the newest release, v2.20.0, still requires x/image
# v0.41.0 (and Go 1.27). Remove once a go-test-coverage release that builds on
# the image's Go requires x/image >= 0.45.0 (>= 0.43.0 for CVE-2026-46602).
CVE-2026-46602
CVE-2026-46603

# =============================================================================
# golang.org/x/mod < 0.40.0 vendored in prebuilt Go CLIs. The deferred pair
# from the Go 1.26.6 / 1.25.13 batch (#559), which held them back while no
# carrier reported a vulnerable x/mod; Trivy's DB has since ingested them and
# they now gate every image that carries one. Issue #567.
#
# Vulnerable code is golang.org/x/mod/sumdb — the Go module CHECKSUM-DATABASE
# CLIENT: a malicious GOSUMDB could serve module content absent from the
# transparency log, and a coordinating GOPROXY/GOSUMDB pair could forge sumdb
# responses. Carriers as of the 2026-10-21 audit (issue #629):
#   - tofu 1.13.9 (dev-base), x/mod v0.39.0. tofu is not a Go module client:
#     it never fetches Go modules from a GOPROXY or verifies them against a
#     GOSUMDB. (The release binary is stripped, so `go tool nm` cannot list
#     its linked packages.)
#   - go-licenses v2.0.1 (dev-go), x/mod v0.27.0. The only x/mod package linked
#     into the binary is x/mod/semver (`go tool nm`); x/mod/sumdb is not in it.
# Corroboration from the scans themselves: /usr/local/go/bin/go, the one real
# module client in these images, is NOT flagged — the toolchain already ships
# the patched x/mod. gh, scorecard, trivy and the other go-install linters
# already require x/mod >= 0.40.0.
#
# Remove per carrier as each upstream re-releases with x/mod >= 0.40.0; watch
# tofu and go-licenses on the weekly bump.
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-56864
CVE-2026-56865

# google.golang.org/grpc v1.83.1 in /usr/local/bin/tofu 1.13.9 (dev-base),
# fixed in 1.83.2. Issue #605; tofu 1.13.2 still shipped v1.83.1 at the issue
# #629 audit, and so does 1.13.9, the newest release (build info in the
# release binary, issue #755).
# CVE-2026-84445: a gRPC-Go server built with
# xds.NewGRPCServer panics on a request that has neither :authority nor Host.
# tofu uses gRPC only as the client of its provider plugins (go-plugin); it
# runs no xDS gRPC server. Remove once a tofu release ships grpc >= 1.83.2.
CVE-2026-84445

# github.com/go-jose/go-jose/v4 < 4.1.6 (dev-base), fixed in 4.1.6 (released
# 2026-10-14). Issue #732; first gated the 2026-10-28 nightly. Carriers, each
# the newest upstream release (checked 2026-10-28; re-checked 2026-11-07,
# issue #755):
#   - /usr/local/bin/scorecard 5.6.0, go-jose v4.1.4
#   - /usr/local/bin/tofu 1.13.9, go-jose v4.1.4
# trivy carried it too (0.76.1, go-jose v4.1.5). The trivy 0.76.2 bump
# (issue #755) ships go-jose v4.1.6, so that carrier is not ignored.
# CVE-2026-116587 — go-jose parses RSA modulus and prime values from a JWK
#   without size bounds before crypto/rsa.PrivateKey.Validate, so a crafted
#   JWK with large or degenerate RSA private parameters costs cubic CPU time.
#   The fix bounds the parameters and rejects private keys embedded in JWS/JWE
#   headers.
# The release binaries link only go-jose's JWK and JWK-set code
# (JSONWebKey.UnmarshalJSON, JSONWebKeySet.Key, Thumbprint, …). None of them
# links ParseSigned, ParseEncrypted or the JWS/JWE header parsers (symbol names
# in each binary, checked 2026-10-28), so the embedded-header path the fix also
# closes is absent. The stripped binaries do not show which caller reaches the
# JWK parser. In these dependency trees JWKs come from key sets fetched over
# TLS (OIDC issuers, signing-key services), so the authenticated endpoint
# would itself have to be malicious and serve private RSA parameters where a
# public key belongs. The impact is CPU exhaustion of a short-lived,
# user-invoked CLI, with no confidentiality or integrity impact. The images
# install tofu for `fmt -check` and `init -backend=false && validate` (no
# backend, no cloud auth; common/opentofu.dockerfile), which fetch no key sets.
# Not fixable by bumping: no newer release of either carrier exists. Remove per
# carrier once a scorecard or tofu release ships go-jose >= 4.1.6; the
# daily upstream-refresh PR picks up the new release.
CVE-2026-116587

# =============================================================================
# undici bundled in npm, fixed in 6.29.1 / 7.30.1 / 8.12.2. Issue #677.
# Carrier: undici 6.28.0 in npm 11.19.1, the npm bundled in Node 24.22.2, at
#   /opt/node/24/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/undici (dev-ts-node:24).
#   Epic vergil-project/.github#649 (vergil-containers#786): the family Node is
#   the nodejs.org tarball pinned in docker/pins/toolchains.yml, and its npm is
#   the runtime's, never upgraded in place (spec §5.8). 24.22.2 is the newest
#   Node 24 (nodejs.org index, checked 2026-11-10). dev-ts-node:22's npm 10.9.9
#   bundles no undici.
# No image installs npm with `npm install -g npm@latest` any more: ts-node was
# the last (it now keeps its Node's own npm), so the earlier npm 12.2.1 carrier
# is gone. dev-base's core Node keeps the npm it bundles, which carries none of
# these: see the npm 10.9.9 group below.
#
# CVE-2026-109869 — undici fetch(): a malicious server that returns a response
#   with more than five content codings and then closes the connection before
#   the body crashes the Node.js process with an unhandled stream error.
# CVE-2026-87018 — undici: a TLS 1.2 server that renegotiates after the
#   connection is established and presents a different CA-trusted certificate
#   whose hostname does not match crashes the Node.js process on an uncaught
#   assertion. Issue #732 (first gated the 2026-10-28 nightly). TLS 1.3 cannot
#   renegotiate, so only a TLS 1.2 endpoint that is itself malicious can
#   trigger it.
# CVE-2026-109383 — undici Agent: a function-valued `tls` option (such as a
#   custom checkServerIdentity) is dropped by a JSON clone, so a pinning
#   callback silently never runs. Issue #732. Only callers that pass a `tls`
#   option to Agent are affected. node-gyp 12.4.0's createDispatcher() passes
#   none: it builds a bare `new Agent()`, or an EnvHttpProxyAgent configured
#   through `connect`, `requestTls` and `proxyTls` (the advisory's own
#   workaround), and it sets no checkServerIdentity at all (lib/download.js in
#   npm 11.19.1, checked 2026-11-10 in the built image). The vulnerable path is
#   not exercised.
# In npm's bundled tree the only package that requires undici is node-gyp
# (12.4.0 in npm 11.19.1). Its lib/download.js uses
# undici's fetch() for one job: downloading the
# Node.js header tarball and SHASUMS256.txt (process.release.headersUrl, by
# default https://nodejs.org) when an install compiles a native addon from
# source and the headers are not yet cached. npm's registry traffic goes through
# make-fetch-happen / minipass-fetch, which do not use undici, so `npm install`
# and `npm ci` of pure-JS packages never reach the vulnerable code. The real
# exposure is in dev-ts-node, where consumers run npm at container runtime: an
# install that builds a native addon fetches headers through this code. To
# trigger the crash, the TLS-authenticated header server (nodejs.org, or a
# configured --dist-url or proxy) must itself be malicious. The impact is a
# crash of a short-lived, user-invoked install, with no confidentiality or
# integrity impact. The same reasoning covers CVE-2026-87018 (a crash of the
# same short-lived install, needing a malicious TLS 1.2 header server).
#
# Remove all three once dev-ts-node:24 no longer carries them (undici >= 6.29.1
# fixes every one): once a Node 24 release bundles an npm that does (the daily
# upstream refresh moves the ts-node:24 pin to the newest 24.x), or once
# ts-node drops Node 24.
# Do not patch npm's bundled node_modules in place.
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-109869
CVE-2026-87018
CVE-2026-109383

# =============================================================================
# undici 6.28.0 in npm 11.19.1, the npm bundled in Node 24.22.2, at
# /opt/node/24/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/undici (dev-ts-node:24 only).
# Fixed in 6.28.1 / 7.29.1 / 8.10.2. Epic vergil-project/.github#649
# (vergil-containers#786; found by the spike, vergil-project/.github#982). The
# carrier is the same as in the group above: the pinned nodejs.org runtime,
# whose npm is never upgraded in place (spec §5.8), and 24.22.2 is the newest
# Node 24 (checked 2026-11-10).
#
# CVE-2026-19534 — undici's WebSocket client crashes the Node.js process during
#   the opening handshake when the server answers with a subprotocol the client
#   never requested.
# Only undici's WebSocket client is affected. npm's only undici user, node-gyp
# 12.4.0, imports Agent, EnvHttpProxyAgent, RetryAgent and fetch from undici
# (lib/download.js) and opens no WebSocket; nothing else in npm requires undici
# (checked 2026-11-10 in the built image). The vulnerable path is not
# exercised. The impact would anyway be a crash of a short-lived, user-invoked
# npm process, with no confidentiality or integrity impact.
# Remove once a Node 24 release bundles an npm carrying undici >= 6.28.1 (the
# daily upstream refresh moves the ts-node:24 pin to the newest 24.x), or once
# ts-node drops Node 24. Do not patch npm's bundled node_modules in place.
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-19534

# =============================================================================
# npm bundled in the nodejs.org Node tarballs pinned in
# docker/pins/toolchains.yml. Epic vergil-project/.github#649 (found by the
# spike, vergil-project/.github#982). Carriers:
#   - npm 10.9.9 in the core Node 22.23.4 (dev-base, and every image built on
#     it), at /opt/vergil/node/22/lib/node_modules/npm/
#     (common/core-node.dockerfile; vergil-containers#779): every ID below.
#   - the same npm 10.9.9 in the family Node 22.23.4 of dev-ts-node:22, at
#     /opt/node/22/lib/node_modules/npm/ (vergil-containers#786): every ID
#     below.
#   - npm 11.19.1 in the family Node 24.22.2 of dev-ts-node:24, at
#     /opt/node/24/lib/node_modules/npm/ (vergil-containers#786):
#     CVE-2026-102276 and CVE-2026-102278 only, in its brace-expansion 5.0.9
#     (fixed in 5.0.10 and 5.0.11).
# Each npm is its runtime's: it is never upgraded in place (spec §5.8), so a
# fix arrives only with a Node release. 22.23.4 and 24.22.2 are the newest of
# their majors (nodejs.org index, checked 2026-11-10), so there is no runtime
# to move to within either major. Confirmed by Trivy 0.76.2 scans of
# /opt/node/<major> in each locally built arm64 image (2026-11-10). All HIGH,
# all in packages npm vendors; none is in Node itself or markdownlint-cli:
# CVE-2026-102276, CVE-2026-102278, CVE-2026-13149, CVE-2026-14257,
# CVE-2026-69152 — brace-expansion 2.0.2 (fixed in 2.1.2 to 2.1.6 by ID):
#   denial of service (stack, memory or CPU exhaustion) from a crafted brace
#   pattern.
# CVE-2026-33671 — picomatch 4.0.3 (fixed in 4.0.4): regular-expression
#   denial of service from a crafted extglob pattern.
# CVE-2026-48815 — sigstore 3.1.0 (fixed in 4.1.1): the certificateOIDs
#   verification option is ignored, so an unintended certificate is accepted.
# CVE-2026-69192 — ip-address 10.1.0 (fixed in 10.3.1): inconsistent address
#   parsing that can bypass an SSRF or trust-boundary check.
# CVE-2026-9496 — pacote 19.0.2 and 20.0.1 (fixed in 21.5.1): denial of
#   service from a crafted spec.rawSpec in a git dependency.
# The vulnerable paths are not exercised. npm runs once, at image build, to
# install markdownlint-cli (pure JS) from the public registry by name: no
# attacker-supplied glob or brace pattern, git spec, address or provenance check
# reaches it. At run time the core Node is not on PATH (no node, npm or npx;
# checks-defaults.sh asserts it), and the only thing that runs on it is the
# markdownlint wrapper, which loads markdownlint-cli and never npm. A consumer
# would have to call /opt/vergil/node/22/bin/npm by path, which nothing does.
# Every finding is a denial of service of a build-time step except
# CVE-2026-48815, and npm 10.9.9 runs no sigstore verification on that install
# (no `npm audit signatures`, no provenance check). Moving the core Node to 24
# would leave three of the IDs, and a core move is a reviewed PR of its own
# (spec §5.2.1).
# dev-ts-node is different: its family Node's npm is the image's default npm,
# and consumers run it at container runtime (vergil-tooling's TypeScript checks
# run `npm ci` and `npm audit --audit-level=high`, and a developer may run any
# npm command). Per finding, in that npm (checked 2026-11-10 in the built
# images):
#   - brace-expansion (the five IDs) is reached through minimatch, which expands
#     the glob patterns of the project's own `workspaces`, `npm query` and
#     `npm diff` arguments, and the `files` and .npmignore patterns of a package
#     npm packs: the project itself, or a git or directory dependency at
#     install. picomatch is reached only through tinyglobby in node-gyp's
#     build.js, with node-gyp's own fixed patterns. A crafted pattern can come
#     only from the developer's own project or from a dependency the developer
#     chose to install, and a git dependency already runs its own prepare
#     script at install, which is far more than a denial of service. The impact
#     is CPU or memory exhaustion of a short-lived, user-invoked npm process.
#   - pacote's CVE-2026-9496 needs a crafted git dependency spec, which again
#     comes from the project's or a chosen dependency's package.json; the
#     impact is the same denial of service.
#   - sigstore's CVE-2026-48815 makes sigstore ignore a caller's
#     certificateOIDs option. npm (pacote's attestation check, used by
#     `npm audit signatures`) passes no certificateOIDs option to
#     sigstore.verify, so its verification is unchanged.
#   - ip-address is required only by the socks client, which parses the address
#     of a SOCKS proxy the developer configured; no attacker-supplied address
#     reaches it.
# Remove each once no carrier is left: the core Node's and dev-ts-node:22's
# once a Node 22 release bundles an npm carrying its fixed package (the daily
# upstream refresh moves the core Node pin and the ts-node:22 pin to the newest
# 22.x), or once the core Node moves to a major whose npm carries them all and
# ts-node drops Node 22; dev-ts-node:24's (CVE-2026-102276, CVE-2026-102278)
# once a Node 24 release bundles an npm with brace-expansion >= 5.0.11, or once
# ts-node drops Node 24. Do not patch npm's bundled node_modules in place.
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-102276
CVE-2026-102278
CVE-2026-13149
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152
CVE-2026-33671
CVE-2026-48815
CVE-2026-69192
CVE-2026-9496

# =============================================================================
# krb5-libs 1.21.1-10.el9_8.1 in the UBI 9 base (dev-pkg-rhel:9), fixed in
# 1.21.1-10.el9_9.2 (RHSA-2026:99715). Issue #866; first gated the 2026-11-13
# CD run. MIT fixed the batch in krb5 1.22.3 (MITKRB5-SA-2026-001,
# https://web.mit.edu/kerberos/advisories/MITKRB5-SA-2026-001.txt). Not
# fixable by rebuilding: the image's daily `dnf upgrade -y` runs, but the UBI 9
# BaseOS repository still offers only krb5-libs 1.21.1-10.el9_8.1 (repodata
# checked 2026-11-13).
#
# The image runs no Kerberos service. It installs no krb5-server (krb5kdc,
# kadmind), libkadm5, krb5-workstation or krb5-pkinit, and nothing it installs
# requires them (UBI 9 BaseOS repodata). krb5-libs is there because libcurl,
# which curl and git use, links libgssapi_krb5 and libkrb5 (with libk5crypto
# and libkrb5support). Nothing in the image requires libgssrpc or libkdb5, the
# other krb5-libs libraries. Each CVE below is in code that only a KDC, kadmind
# or a GSS-RPC server runs. The file is the one MIT's fix commit changes
# (github.com/krb5/krb5); each description is at
# https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/<id>.
# CVE-2026-107364 — KDC read overrun in fetch_asn1_field() (src/kdc/
#   kdc_util.c), part of krb5kdc.
# CVE-2026-71200 — KDC NULL dereference in PKINIT CMS processing, only on a
#   KDC configured for PKINIT. The code is the PKINIT plugin (src/plugins/
#   preauth/pkinit), shipped in krb5-pkinit.
# CVE-2026-112317 — KDC or kadmind memory leak in krb5_ktkdb_get_entry()
#   (src/lib/kdb/keytab.c, libkdb5), which reads keys from the KDC database.
# CVE-2026-112316 — kadmind memory leak in xdr_krb5_tl_data()
#   (src/lib/kadm5/kadm_rpc_xdr.c), in the kadm5 libraries (libkadm5).
# CVE-2026-112318 — kadmind NULL dereference in the policy RPC stubs
#   (src/kadmin/server/server_stubs.c), part of kadmind.
# CVE-2026-112315, CVE-2026-112319, CVE-2026-112320, CVE-2026-112321,
# CVE-2026-112322, CVE-2026-112323 — kadmind memory and CPU exhaustion in
#   libgssrpc's RPC server code and XDR decoding (src/lib/rpc: authgss_prot.c,
#   svc_auth_gss.c, svc_auth.c, svc_auth_gssapi.c, xdr.c; CVE-2026-112319 also
#   in src/lib/kadm5).
# CVE-2026-118380 — the RPCSEC_GSS server uses an unverified service level
#   (src/lib/rpc/svc_auth_gss.c), so an on-path attacker can alter kadmind or
#   iprop RPC arguments or have replies sent in plain text.
# No process in the image accepts Kerberos, kadmin or GSS-RPC traffic, so none
# of these paths can run.
#
# CVE-2026-119079 and CVE-2026-71199 are not in this group. Both are fixed in
# libkrb5 itself (src/lib/krb5/asn.1/asn1_encode.c and
# src/lib/krb5/krb/cammac_util.c), the library curl and git load, so they
# await a ruling on issue #866.
#
# Remove the group once the UBI 9 BaseOS repository ships krb5-libs
# >= 1.21.1-10.el9_9.2 and a fresh dev-pkg-rhel:9 build scans clean without it.
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-107364
CVE-2026-71200
CVE-2026-112315
CVE-2026-112316
CVE-2026-112317
CVE-2026-112318
CVE-2026-112319
CVE-2026-112320
CVE-2026-112321
CVE-2026-112322
CVE-2026-112323
CVE-2026-118380
